    <item>
      <title>tommy needs a haircut</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/tommy-needs-a-haircut/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 10 Mar 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/tommy-needs-a-haircut/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;A series of ongoing live works centred on the world of Grand Theft Auto: Vice City. This work began in March 2024 as a playful revisitation of a nostalgic game from my childhood. I employ the protagonist, Tommy, as the actor on my stage who performs in ways that are often more sensual than originally written in the game. By doing so, I amplify the complexities of human behaviour and social dynamics within the game environment as they reflect real-world ethical dilemmas fuelled with existentialism. Inspired by Lev Manovich&amp;rsquo;s notions of media remixability, I am interested in remixing not just aesthetics but also techniques, methods, and languages of different media. For the future of this project, I want to get into subtle alterations of the game world itself.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>LyrArkestra&#43;</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/lyra/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 18 Nov 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/lyra/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;LyrArkestra+ was a collaborative project within which I created visuals along with &lt;a
  href=&#34;https://cristinamaldonado.com&#34;
    target=&#34;_blank&#34;
  &gt;Cristina&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a
  href=&#34;https://isajuchniewicz.com&#34;
    target=&#34;_blank&#34;
  &gt;Isa&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The project focused on performing graphic scores primarily by Czech and Slovak composers in unconventional audiovisual renditions. The international ensemble of this essentially fluid project does not have a permanent team. The audio composition were developed and performed by Tomáš Knoflíček (Gurun Gurun) from Ostrava, Michal Zbořil (IQ+1, B4) from Přerov, Daniel Jakeš (Jasnovidec, Koroze) from High Tatras, Ken Ganfield (PIO, The MoND) from Ames, Martin Nábělek (Boyse) from Banská Bystrica, and Petr Vrba (Poisonous Frequencies, Banausoi) from Prague. All sounds originated in the Lyra synthesizer, which is described as &amp;ldquo;organismic&amp;rdquo;, i.e. close to living organisms in its internal interactions and functioning on the basis of imaginary &amp;ldquo;conversations&amp;rdquo; between the individual modules&amp;hellip;The musical component is complemented by the visuals of Cristina Maldonado, Keya Singh and Isa Juchniewicz, who has created a structured digital environment that both responds directly to the music and allows for an additional layer of improvisation.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Insomnia Festival 2021</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/insomnia21/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 02 Oct 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/insomnia21/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I was invited to create visuals for 3 sets back-to-back for Insomnia Festival&amp;rsquo;s kick-off event at Storgata Camping (Tromsø, Norway). The first two sets lasted about 1 hour each while the last one was 3 hours long.
So far the longest set I have made, this was a great opportunity to see how far I can go with maintaining a sense of live-ness and control even when the material feels like it has already been exhausted.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
